Subject: [PATCH] Reload the running firewall without writing configuration

The reload command toggles ENABLED and regenerates user rules for logging.
Use ufw-init force-reload, which already reloads the configured rules and
runs the framework hooks. This also works on an immutable image.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/backend_iptables.py
+++ b/src/backend_iptables.py
@@ -491,5 +491,12 @@
     def stop_firewall(self):
         '''Stop the firewall'''
+        self._run_init('force-stop')
+
+    def reload_firewall(self):
+        '''Reload the installed rules without changing persistent configuration.'''
+        self._run_init('force-reload')
+
+    def _run_init(self, action):
         if self.dryrun:
             msg("> " + _("running ufw-init"))
         else:
